### Tracking — profile, targets, diary. Set @host from the Aspire dashboard's "api" endpoint.
@host = https://localhost:7443
@subject = demo-user
@today = 2026-06-23

### Set / update the profile (golden worked example → target 2345 kcal). Recomputes the target.
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/profile
X-Debug-Subject: {{subject}}
X-Debug-Role: user
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sex": "Male",
  "birthDate": "1996-06-23",
  "heightCm": 180,
  "weightKg": 80,
  "bodyFatPct": null,
  "activity": "ModeratelyActive",
  "goal": "ModerateCut",
  "macroStrategy": "ProteinAnchored",
  "allergens": ["peanuts"],
  "dislikes": ["mushrooms"],
  "preferredDiets": []
}

### Get the current profile
GET {{host}}/api/v1/profile
X-Debug-Subject: {{subject}}

### Get the derived daily target
GET {{host}}/api/v1/targets
X-Debug-Subject: {{subject}}

### Log a diary entry (foodId + portionId come from a foods/search result)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/diary
X-Debug-Subject: {{subject}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "{{today}}",
  "mealSlot": "Breakfast",
  "foodId": "REPLACE-WITH-FOOD-ID",
  "portionId": "REPLACE-WITH-PORTION-ID",
  "quantity": 2
}

### Get the day's diary + rollup vs. target
GET {{host}}/api/v1/diary?date={{today}}
X-Debug-Subject: {{subject}}

### 7-day calorie trend
GET {{host}}/api/v1/diary/trend?days=7
X-Debug-Subject: {{subject}}

### Natural-language logging → confirmable candidates (needs an LLM provider; else 503)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/diary/parse
X-Debug-Subject: {{subject}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "2 eggs and a banana", "mealSlot": "Breakfast" }

### Barcode lookup (fetch-on-miss from Open Food Facts; seeded GTIN works offline)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/foods/barcode/5449000000996
X-Debug-Subject: {{subject}}

### Anonymous call (no subject header) → expect 401
GET {{host}}/api/v1/targets
